   "text": {
    "L1": "The SI unit of time is the second, written s.",
    "L2": "A simple pendulum has a small heavy bob hanging from a thread.",
    "L3": "One oscillation is one complete swing from one end to the other and back.",
    "L4": "MYTH: a heavier bob makes a pendulum swing faster. Not true: the bob's mass does not change the time period.",
    "L5": "A longer thread gives a longer time period, so it swings more slowly. A shorter thread swings faster.",
    "L6": "To measure accurately, time several oscillations and divide the total time by their number.",
    "L7": "For example, 10 oscillations take 18 seconds. The time period is 18 divided by 10, or 1.8 seconds.",
    "L8": "Now check your understanding: choose the correct time period."
   },
